  "prefLabel": "Puc 1302.06 Federal Communications Commission (FCC)",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Puc 1302.06 “Federal Communications Commission (FCC)” means the U.S. government agency established by the Communications Act of 1934 and charged with regulating interstate and international communications by radio, television, wire, satellite, and cable.\n\nSource. #9614, eff 12-12-09; ss by #12574, eff 9-1-18; ss by #13498, eff 12-1-22 (formerly Puc 1302.07) (See Revision Note at chapter heading for Puc 1300)",
